WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.558
High heels were made for men on

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.475
horseback.

00:00:02.485 --> 00:00:04.823
Persian riders wore heels so their feet

00:00:04.833 --> 00:00:06.594
sat firmly in the stirrups.

00:00:06.604 --> 00:00:09.069
Standing up, a rider could steady himself

00:00:09.079 --> 00:00:10.558
and shoot his bow better.

00:00:10.568 --> 00:00:13.700
Around 1600, as Persian
envoys reached Europe,

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.341
aristocrats there copied the shoes.

00:00:16.441 --> 00:00:17.864
Here's the real look:

00:00:17.874 --> 00:00:20.999
King Louis the Fourteenth,
painted in 1701.

00:00:21.009 --> 00:00:21.875
Red heels.

00:00:21.975 --> 00:00:23.838
Only men in the king's favour were

00:00:23.848 --> 00:00:25.564
allowed to wear the red heel.

00:00:25.574 --> 00:00:27.386
Then women took up heels too.

00:00:27.396 --> 00:00:29.960
And by the 1700s, high heels counted

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.274
as women's shoes.

00:00:31.392 --> 00:00:33.082
So every stiletto started out on a

00:00:33.092 --> 00:00:34.317
Persian rider.

00:00:34.342 --> 00:00:34.970
Yes:

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.142
high heels...
